               "caution":  "The stock\u0027s sharp rebound on November 23 came on below-average volume (44.26M vs 46.30M) and was driven by Nvidia-linked sector sentiment rather than an Alphabet-specific turnaround. With FY2026 capex guided at $195B–$205B and set to rise further in 2027, negative free cash flow and rising debt ($125.1B plus C$6B in new bonds) leave little room for execution stumbles. Until AI Mode search monetization catches up to legacy ads and price reclaims its $287.71–$311.57 resistance zone, downside retests near $260–$264 remain possible.",
