               "fundamental":  "Alphabet\u0027s Q3 2026 report on October 28 showed an AI-infrastructure powerhouse absorbing an unprecedented investment bill. Consolidated revenue rose 25% YoY to $127.6B and operating income climbed 30% to $40.6B (31.8% margin), though EPS fell to $2.12 partly from non-operating equity markdowns tied to holdings including SpaceX. The standout was Google Cloud, doubling 103% YoY to $30.7B with a 36.2% operating margin and $561B backlog as enterprise AI and external TPU sales scaled. Yet $51.4B in quarterly capex drove -$9.1B free cash flow (following -$5.9B in Q2), prompting a C$6B bond issue on November 19 alongside $125.1B in long-term debt. Coupled with lower near-term monetization in AI Mode search, the stock sold off sharply—reflecting capital-intensity and ROI timing fears rather than damage to its vertically integrated Search, Cloud, TPU, and Gemini moat.",
