               "summary":  "Alphabet (GOOGL) closed at $282.10 on November 23, 2026—up 6.34% in a broad AI relief rally, yet still 31% below its $408.61 52-week high. Shares plunged roughly 12.6% after October 28 Q3 results revealed $51.4B in quarterly capital spending and -$9.1B in free cash flow, alongside a C$6B bond sale priced November 19. Operationally, Google Cloud surged 103% year-over-year to $30.7B with a $561B backlog, while new TPU 8tx/8i Max chips and Gemini 4 reinforced the long-term platform moat. Technically, the trend stays bearish pending a reclaim of key moving averages.",
